<%- include('layout', { body: `
<h2><i class='fas fa-wifi'></i> Tor Access Point</h2>

<div class='card'>
  <h3>Access Point Status</h3>
  <div class='card-content'>
    <div class='grid grid-3'>
      <div class='status-row'><span>Overall:</span><span id='ap-active' class='badge badge-unknown'>Checking...</span></div>
      <div class='status-row'><span>hostapd:</span><span id='ap-hostapd' class='badge badge-unknown'>--</span></div>
      <div class='status-row'><span>dnsmasq:</span><span id='ap-dnsmasq' class='badge badge-unknown'>--</span></div>
      <div class='status-row'><span>Tor:</span><span id='ap-tor' class='badge badge-unknown'>--</span></div>
      <div class='status-row'><span>SSID:</span><span id='ap-ssid'>--</span></div>
      <div class='status-row'><span>Clients:</span><span id='ap-clients'>--</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class='btn-group' style='margin-top: 1.5rem;'>
      <button class='btn btn-success btn-lg' onclick='apAction(\"start\")'><i class='fas fa-play'></i> Start Tor AP</button>
      <button class='btn btn-danger btn-lg' onclick='apAction(\"stop\")'><i class='fas fa-stop'></i> Stop Tor AP</button>
    </div>
    <div id='ap-message' class='message' style='margin-top: 0.5rem;'></div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class='card'>
  <h3><i class='fas fa-plane'></i> WiFi-to-WiFi Travel Mode</h3>
  <div class='card-content'>
    <div class='info-box' style='margin-bottom: 1rem;'>
      <p><strong>Travel Mode</strong> uses a USB WiFi adapter to connect to an upstream WiFi network, then creates a Tor AP on the built-in wlan0. This turns your Pi into a portable Tor router — no Ethernet cable needed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class='grid grid-2'>
      <div>
        <h4 style='margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>Step 1 — Detect USB Adapter</h4>
        <button class='btn btn-primary' onclick='scanUsbAdapters()'><i class='fas fa-search'></i> Search WiFi-2-WiFi USB Adapter</button>
        <div id='usb-scan-result' style='margin-top: 0.5rem;'></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4 style='margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>Travel Mode Status</h4>
        <div id='travel-status'>
          <span class='badge badge-unknown'>Not checked</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id='travel-config' style='display: none; margin-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 1rem;'>
      <h4 style='margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>Step 2 — Connect to upstream WiFi</h4>
      <div class='form-group'>
        <label for='travel-iface'>USB WiFi Interface</label>
        <select id='travel-iface' class='form-control'><option value=''>Select adapter...</option></select>
      </div>
      <div class='btn-group' style='margin-bottom: 1rem;'>
        <button class='btn btn-primary btn-sm' onclick='scanWifiNetworks()'><i class='fas fa-broadcast-tower'></i> Scan WiFi Networks</button>
      </div>
      <div id='wifi-networks' style='margin-bottom: 1rem;'></div>
      <div class='form-group'>
        <label for='travel-ssid'>Upstream WiFi SSID</label>
        <input type='text' id='travel-ssid' class='form-control' placeholder='WiFi network name'>
      </div>
      <div class='form-group'>
        <label for='travel-pass'>Upstream WiFi Password</label>
        <input type='password' id='travel-pass' class='form-control' placeholder='Leave empty for open networks'>
      </div>
      <div class='btn-group'>
        <button class='btn btn-success' onclick='startTravelMode()'><i class='fas fa-play'></i> Start Travel Mode</button>
        <button class='btn btn-danger' onclick='stopTravelMode()'><i class='fas fa-stop'></i> Stop Travel Mode</button>
      </div>
      <div id='travel-message' class='message' style='margin-top: 0.5rem;'></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class='card'>
  <h3><i class='fas fa-info-circle'></i> How it works</h3>
  <div class='card-content'>
    <div class='info-box'>
      <p>When activated, the Tor Access Point:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Creates a WiFi hotspot on <strong>wlan0</strong> with the configured SSID and passphrase.</li>
        <li>Assigns IP addresses to connected clients via <strong>dnsmasq</strong> DHCP.</li>
        <li>Redirects all TCP traffic through the <strong>Tor</strong> transparent proxy.</li>
        <li>Routes all DNS queries through Tor DNS resolver (prevents leaks).</li>
        <li>Blocks UDP traffic (Tor only supports TCP).</li>
        <li><strong>Captive Portal:</strong> Devices connecting to the hotspot are automatically redirected to the dashboard login page.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Any device</strong> connected to this hotspot automatically gets Tor anonymization.</p>
      <p><strong>Travel Mode</strong> adds WiFi-to-WiFi: USB adapter connects to upstream WiFi, built-in wlan0 becomes the AP.</p>
      <p class='text-warning'><i class='fas fa-exclamation-triangle'></i> Internet speeds will be slower through Tor. Some sites may block Tor exit nodes.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script src='/js/ap.js'></script>
` }) %>
